# Woody — Engine Rules

> **Repo:** TypeScript engine in `lib/`, `app/api/`, `packages/shared/`; Python acoustic service in `packages/acoustic-service/`. See `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_SSOT.md` and `WOODY_BUILD_SPEC.md` (canonical engineering reference).

---

## CRITICAL ARCHITECTURE — READ FIRST

**Woody is a navigation engine, not a recommendation engine.** It takes acoustic coordinate instructions and finds a path. The distinction matters in every naming decision, every API contract, every comment.

### The 4-Layer Stack

```
Layer 0  Raw audio
Layer 1  Essentia signal features ~400D (deterministic extraction)
Layer 2  CLAP embeddings 512D  ← PRIMARY NAVIGATION LAYER
         model: laion/larger_clap_music_and_speech
         multimodal: text "late night drive" and matching audio are close in this space
Layer 3  5D perceptual projection  ← DISPLAY ONLY (lossy, user-facing)
```

**Layer 2 is where all navigation happens.** Arc generation, k-NN search, territory computation, cold start — all operate on 512-dim CLAP vectors using cosine similarity.

**Layer 3 (5D) is a display output only.** It is computed from CLAP embeddings via linear probe (Phase 2) or heuristic formula (Phase 1). It is never used as a navigation target. Never feed 5D coordinates into a distance function for arc selection.

